Given, equation of parabola is $y^{2}=4 a x \quad \text{...(i)}$
Differentiating $\mathrm{E} \mathrm{g}$. (i) w.r.t. $x$, we get $\begin{aligned}2 y \frac{d y}{d x}&=4 a \\
\Rightarrow \quad \frac{d y}{d x}&=\frac{2 a}{y} \Rightarrow a=\frac{y}{2} \frac{d y}{d x}
\end{aligned}$ Substituting the value of $a$ in Eq. (i), we get $\begin{aligned} y^{2} &=4 \cdot \frac{y}{2} \frac{d y}{d x} x \\
